  "explanation": "<h3>Signed material price variance</h3><p>3,200 × ($5.75 − $6.00) = −$800, favorable.</p><h3>Signed material quantity variance</h3><p>$6 × (3,200 − 3,000) = $1,200, unfavorable.</p><h3>Net material cost variance</h3><p>−$800 + $1,200 = $400 unfavorable.</p><h3>Recommended interpretation</h3><p>The favorable price is offset by usage and potentially quality costs.</p>"
